; tiers.eval — the SAME encounter at two tiers. This is the shape every
; progression-ladder rung will have: seed a party, build the room, place the
; monsters, run a fixed span, print both sides before and after.
;
; The comparison is the artefact. One tier's numbers say nothing on their own;
; two tiers against identical monsters, identical geometry and an identical seed
; say what the seeding was worth.

logecho on
newgame
timescale 0
lockstep on

; --- rung 1: novice -------------------------------------------------------
seed 101
include presets/novice.eval
arena open 9 9
spawn skeleton 14 9 south
tp 14 12
echo === novice vs 1 skeleton: before ===
char 0
party
step 30
echo === novice vs 1 skeleton: after ===
party
monsters

; --- rung 2: veteran, same fight -----------------------------------------
; `heal` FIRST, and it is not optional: rung 1 wipes, a wipe returns to the title
; screen, and every `step` after that is correctly refused — the first version of
; this script measured nothing at all from here down. Heal restores the party in
; place without disturbing what a preset seeded.
;
; A fresh arena wipes the previous encounter, and the same seed makes the dice
; the same dice — so any difference is the seeding and nothing else.
heal
seed 101
include presets/veteran.eval
arena open 9 9
spawn skeleton 14 9 south
tp 14 12
echo === veteran vs 1 skeleton: before ===
char 0
party
step 30
echo === veteran vs 1 skeleton: after ===
party
monsters
state
